      "kind": "greeting",
      "start": 0.63,
      "end": 2.41,
      "text": "Hello! How's everything today?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 9.74,
      "end": 14.9,
      "text": "It's easier than it sounds. Do you have jump leads, and is your car parked close enough to reach her battery?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 19.1,
      "end": 30.01,
      "text": "Perfect. Both engines off first. Red clamp goes on her positive terminal, then your positive. Black goes on your negative, and the last black clamp on bare metal on her engine, away from the battery."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 38.401,
      "end": 44.911,
      "text": "It's a safety thing. The final connection can spark, and batteries can give off gas, so you want that spark away from it."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 48.381,
      "end": 54.551,
      "text": "Yes, let yours run for a few minutes, then try hers. Once it starts, take the clamps off in the reverse order."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 57.911,
      "end": 65.021,
      "text": "Ideally for half an hour or so, to put some charge back in. If it dies again tomorrow, the battery probably needs replacing."
    }
  ]
